<h2 id="boox-picco-unveiled">Onyx Boox Picco: A New Pocket E-Reader</h2>

<p>Onyx Boox has teased a new pocket-sized e-reader called the <strong>BOOX Picco</strong>, marking the company's entry into the ultra-portable e-reader segment. First reported by Good e-Reader on July 23, 2026, the Picco is a 3.97-inch black-and-white E Ink device designed to compete directly with the XTEINK line of pocket readers that have gone viral for their magnetic, phone-attached form factor.</p>

<p>The Picco is the first device in Onyx Boox's new <strong>Tile product line</strong>, which appears to focus on compact, task-specific E Ink devices rather than full-featured Android e-readers. This represents a strategic shift for Onyx Boox, a company better known for large-format note-taking devices like the Note Air and Tab series, as well as the smartphone-sized Palma 2.</p>

<p>For EPUB readers, the Picco is especially interesting. A pocket-sized device that natively supports EPUB — without the distractions of a smartphone — could be the ideal companion for commuters, digital minimalists, and anyone who wants to carry an entire EPUB library in a tiny package.</p>

<h2 id="specs-and-features">What We Know About the BOOX Picco</h2>

<p>Onyx Boox has not published a full spec sheet yet, but teaser images and leaks reveal several confirmed and rumored features:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Feature</th>
      <th>Details</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Display</strong></td>
      <td>3.97-inch black-and-white E Ink with front light</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Page Turn Buttons</strong></td>
      <td>Physical buttons visible on teaser images</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Storage</strong></td>
      <td>Expandable via SD card slot</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Touchscreen</strong></td>
      <td>Likely not included (to keep cost low)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>UI</strong></td>
      <td>Custom Tile UI — reading, music, podcast focused</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Expected Price</strong></td>
      <td>$99 — $129 USD</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Product Line</strong></td>
      <td>First device in the new "Tile" series</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>The absence of a touchscreen on a sub-$100 device would be a notable tradeoff. Page-turn buttons handle navigation, but tasks like selecting text, adjusting font size, or managing bookmarks would require on-device controls. This tradeoff is similar to the approach XTEINK takes with its pocket readers — keep the hardware simple and focused on one thing: reading.</p>

<p>The SD card slot is a strong feature for EPUB readers. A 3.97-inch E Ink screen with a 512GB SD card could theoretically hold tens of thousands of EPUB files. Combined with the front light, reading in the dark is fully supported, unlike some ultra-budget e-readers that omit this feature.</p>

<h2 id="vs-xteink">BOOX Picco vs XTEINK: Pocket Reader Comparison</h2>

<p>XTEINK has dominated the pocket e-reader space in 2026 with its magnetic, MagSafe-attached devices starting at $99. The X4 Pro, XTEINK's latest model, is a 4-inch reader that magnetically snaps to the back of an iPhone or Android phone, effectively turning your smartphone into an e-reader case.</p>

<p>Here is how the BOOX Picco compares to the current XTEINK lineup:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Feature</th>
      <th>Onyx Boox Picco</th>
      <th>XTEINK X4 Pro</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Screen Size</strong></td>
      <td>3.97 inches</td>
      <td>~4 inches</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Display Type</strong></td>
      <td>E Ink B&W + front light</td>
      <td>E Ink B&W + front light</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Touchscreen</strong></td>
      <td>Likely no (physical buttons)</td>
      <td>No</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Magnetic Phone Attachment</strong></td>
      <td>Not confirmed</td>
      <td>Yes (MagSafe)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>SD Card Slot</strong></td>
